# CentOS Linux Installation Lab

## Overview

This project documents the installation and configuration of a CentOS Linux virtual machine. The objective was to gain practical experience deploying an enterprise Linux operating system and understanding Linux boot processes and storage configuration.

## Environment

* Hypervisor: Microsoft Hyper-V
* Operating System: CentOS Linux
* Virtual Machine Type: Generation 2
* Virtual Storage: VHDX
* Virtual Network: Hyper-V Default Switch

## Project Objectives

* Install CentOS Linux.
* Configure default disk partitions.
* Understand Linux filesystem structure.
* Explore GRUB bootloader functionality.
* Validate successful system deployment.

## Installation Process

### 1. Virtual Machine Creation

Created a dedicated virtual machine and attached the CentOS installation ISO.

### 2. Operating System Installation

Configured:

* Default partition layout
* Root filesystem
* Boot partition
* Standard installation options

### 3. Initial Configuration

Completed:

* User configuration
* System setup
* Bootloader installation

### 4. Validation

Verified successful deployment by logging into the operating system and executing:

```bash
date
```

## Key Concepts Learned

### Linux Filesystems

Gained familiarity with:

* Root filesystem (/)
* Boot partitions
* Linux storage management

### GRUB Bootloader

Studied:

* Linux boot sequence
* GRUB configuration
* Operating system startup process

### Virtualization

Applied:

* Virtual machine deployment
* Virtual disk management
* Hyper-V administration

## Skills Demonstrated

* Linux Administration
* CentOS Installation
* Hyper-V Virtualization
* Operating System Deployment
* Troubleshooting
* Bootloader Configuration
* Technical Documentation

## Lessons Learned

This project provided hands-on experience with enterprise Linux deployment and reinforced core system administration concepts including storage management, boot processes, and virtual machine administration.

